an cause a loss of vehicle control, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"GM will notify owners, and dealers will inspect the tires, replacing them as necessary, free of charge.  The recall began March 22, 2021.  Owners may contact GMC customer service at 1-888-988-7267, Buick customer service at 1-866-608-8080, Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-222-1020 or Cadillac customer service at 1-800-458-8006.  GM's number for this recall is N212329050.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":33838,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=21V115000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":26,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"BLAZER"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TAHOE"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"ACADIA"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"YUKON"},{"year":"2021","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"EXPRESS"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SUBURBAN"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"YUKON XL"},{"year":"2020","make":"CADILLAC","model":"ESCALADE"},{"year":"2021","make":"GMC","model":"SAVANA"},{"year":"2020","make":"CADILLAC","model":"XT5"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"ACADIA"},{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"BLAZER"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"},{"year":"2020","make":"BUICK","model":"ENCLAVE"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"SAVANA"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"EXPRESS"},{"year":"2020","make":"CADILLAC","model":"ESCALADE ESV"},{"year":"2020","make":"CADILLAC","model":"XT4"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"EXPRESS"},{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"SAVANA"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"21V817000","received":"2021-10-18","manufacturer":"Braun Corporation","component":"POWER TRAIN:AUTOMATIC TRANSMISSION","summary":"Braun Corporation (Braun) is recalling certain 2020-2021 Chevrolet Traverse wheelchair accessible vehicles with Power In-floor Ramp conversion.  The screw and clip that hold the inner wheel-well plastic shroud in place may chafe against the transmission case, possibly resulting in a transmission fluid leak.","consequence":"A transmission fluid leak can cause a loss of drive power, increasing the risk of a crash.  In addition, a leak in the presence of an ignition source increases the risk of a fire.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the screw and clip, and inspect for signs of contact with the transmission, free of charge.  Owner notification letters were mailed November 29, 2021.  Owners may contact Braun customer service at 1-800-488-0359.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":639,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=21V817000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":2,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"},{"year":"2021","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"20V639000","received":"2020-10-15","manufacturer":"General Motors LLC","component":"FUEL SYSTEM, GASOLINE:DELIVERY:FUEL PUMP","summary":"General Motors LLC (GM) is recalling certain 2020 Buick Enclave, Cadillac XT5, Cadillac XT6, Chevrolet Traverse, and GMC Acadia vehicles.  The fuel pump's jet nozzle may have a plastic burr remaining from the manufacturing process, possibly causing a blocked nozzle and an insufficient fuel supply to the engine.","consequence":"Insufficient fuel supply can result in an engine stall without warning, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"GM will notify owners, and dealers will replace the fuel pump module.  The recall began November 16, 2020.  Owners may contact GMC customer service at 1-888-988-7267, Buick Customer service at 1-866-608-8080, Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-222-1020 or Cadillac customer service at 1-800-458-8006.   GM's number for this recall is N202314760.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":2781,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=20V639000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":5,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"ACADIA"},{"year":"2020","make":"CADILLAC","model":"XT5"},{"year":"2020","make":"CADILLAC","model":"XT6"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"},{"year":"2020","make":"BUICK","model":"ENCLAVE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"20V684000","received":"2020-11-05","manufacturer":"General Motors LLC","component":"TIRES","summary":"General Motors LLC (GM) is recalling certain 2020 Buick Enclave, Cadillac XT5, GMC Acadia and Chevrolet Traverse vehicles and 2020-2021 Chevrolet Silverado 1500, GMC Sierra 1500 vehicles.  The vehicles may have been manufactured with Continental tires that were overcured.","consequence":"Overcured tires may experience a carcass break in the sidewall resulting in a sudden air loss or could develop a belt edge separation which could lead to partial or full tread/belt loss.  Either condition increases the risk of a crash.","remedy":"GM will notify owners, and dealers will inspect vehicles and replace tires that have DOT number and production mold number combinations identified by Continental, free of charge.  The recall began December 17, 2020.  Owners may contact GMC customer service at 1-888-988-7267, Buick customer service at 1-866-608-8080, Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-222-1020 or Cadillac customer service at 1-800-458-8006.  GM's number for this recall is N202319030.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":7516,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=20V684000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":8,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"ACADIA"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2020","make":"CADILLAC","model":"XT5"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"},{"year":"2020","make":"BUICK","model":"ENCLAVE"},{"year":"2021","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2021","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"20V446000","received":"2020-07-30","manufacturer":"General Motors LLC","component":"AIR BAGS:SIDE/WINDOW:CURTAIN:INFLATOR","summary":"General Motors, LLC. (GM) is recalling certain 2020 Buick Enclave, Cadillac XT5 and XT6, Chevrolet Blazer, Silverado 1500, 2500 and 3500 and Traverse and GMC Acadia and Sierra 1500, 2500 and 3500 vehicles.  The diffuser component of the Roof-Rail Air Bag (RRAB) inflator may not have been properly crimped to the inflator and could separate from the inflator during air bag deployment.","consequence":"If the diffuser separates from the inflator during deployment, RRAB performance may be degraded, increasing the risk of injury in a crash.","remedy":"GM will notify owners, and dealers will replace the suspect RRAB modules, free of charge.  The recall began September 3, 2020.  Owners may contact Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-630-2438, Cadillac customer service at 1-800-333-4223, or Buick customer service at 1-800-521-7300.  GM's number for this recall is N202305380.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":769,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=20V446000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":12,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"BLAZER"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"ACADIA"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2020","make":"CADILLAC","model":"XT5"},{"year":"2020","make":"CADILLAC","model":"XT6"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 2500"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 3500"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 2500"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 3500"},{"year":"2020","make":"BUICK","model":"ENCLAVE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"20V668000","received":"2020-10-29","manufacturer":"General Motors LLC","component":"POWER TRAIN:AUTOMATIC TRANSMISSION","summary":"General Motors LLC (GM) is recalling certain 2018-2019 Chevrolet Cruze and Buick LaCrosse, 2018-2020 Chevrolet Equinox, Chevrolet Traverse and GMC Terrain, 2018 Chevrolet Malibu, 2019-2020 Buick Encore, Buick Enclave, Cadillac XT4, Chevrolet Blazer and GMC Acadia, and 2020 Cadillac XT6 vehicles.  The start/stop accumulator endcap may have missing bolts.","consequence":"Missing bolts on the start-stop accumulator endcap could result in a transmission oil leak and may progress to a loss of propulsion, increasing the risk of a crash.  A transmission fluid leak in the presence of an ignition source may increase the risk of fire.","remedy":"GM will notify owners, and dealers will inspect the start-stop transmission accumulator and replace it if any bolts are missing, free of charge.  The recall began December 15, 2020.  Owners may contact GMC customer service at 1-888-988-7267, Buick Customer service at 1-866-608-8080, Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-222-1020 or Cadillac customer service at 1-800-458-8006.  GM's number for this recall is N202313440.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":194105,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=20V668000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":25,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"BLAZER"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"ACADIA"},{"year":"2020","make":"CADILLAC","model":"XT6"},{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"TERRAIN"},{"year":"2019","make":"BUICK","model":"LACROSSE"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"EQUINOX"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"},{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"ACADIA"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"CRUZE"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"BLAZER"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"EQUINOX"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"},{"year":"2020","make":"BUICK","model":"ENCLAVE"},{"year":"2019","make":"BUICK","model":"ENCORE"},{"year":"2020","make":"CADILLAC","model":"XT4"},{"year":"2019","make":"CADILLAC","model":"XT4"},{"year":"2019","make":"BUICK","model":"ENCLAVE"},{"year":"2020","make":"BUICK","model":"ENCORE"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"CRUZE"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"MALIBU"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"EQUINOX"},{"year":"2018","make":"BUICK","model":"LACROSSE"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"},{"year":"2018","make":"GMC","model":"TERRAIN"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"19V643000","received":"2019-09-06","manufacturer":"General Motors LLC","component":"STRUCTURE:FRAME AND MEMBERS","summary":"General Motors LLC (GM) is recalling certain 2020 Buick Enclave and Chevrolet Traverse vehicles. The right-hand frame rail in the\r\nengine compartment may be cracked.","consequence":"A crack in the frame rail may reduce crash performance, increasing the risk of an injury.","remedy":"GM will notify owners, and dealers will inspect and, as necessary, replace the vehicle, free of charge.  The recall began October 4, 2019.  Owners may contact Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-630-2438 or Buick customer service at 1-800-521-7300. GM's number for this recall is N192268310.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":3420,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V643000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":2,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"BUICK","model":"ENCLAVE"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"22V210000","received":"2022-03-31","manufacturer":"General Motors, LLC","component":"AIR BAGS:SIDE/WINDOW:CURTAIN","summary":"General Motors, LLC (GM) is recalling certain 2020-2022 Chevrolet Traverse and 2021-2022 Buick Enclave vehicles.  The harness connector to the left or right side roof rail air bag may have incompatible electrical terminals, which could prevent the air bags from deploying in a crash.","consequence":"Roof rail air bags that do not deploy as intended increase the risk of injury in a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the harness connector to the roof rail air bags, free of charge.  Owner notification letters were mailed on April 29, 2022.  Owners may contact Buick customer service at 1-800-521-7300 or Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-222-1020.  GM's number for this recall is N212352140.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":89,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=22V210000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":5,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"},{"year":"2021","make":"BUICK","model":"ENCLAVE"},{"year":"2022","make":"BUICK","model":"ENCLAVE"},{"year":"2022","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"},{"year":"2021","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TRAVERSE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false}]}
